From: Brian 'redbeard' Harrington <redbeard@dead-city.org>
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Platform/Spacemit/K3: Cpu.asl _LPI first cut (Task 9)

Platform/Spacemit/K3: Cpu.asl _LPI first cut (Task 9)

Add _LPI to every ACPI0007 processor device: two non-retentive
platform states per the FFH spec and the HSM suspend audit
(task9-hsm-suspend-audit-2026-11-20.md):

- CPU_NR: FFH address (1<<60)|0x90000000, min-residency 950us,
  wake 500us
- CLUSTER_NR: FFH address (1<<60)|0x91000000, min-residency 2700us,
  wake 1100us

Both use the proven PMU vote + WFI + in-place-resume mechanism from
k3_corepm.c; the kernel's RISC-V LPI backend requires >1 flattened
state, so both are exposed. Package layout per ACPI 6.5 _LPI:
{MinResidency, WakeLatency, Count, StatePkgs...} (iASL-validated).
Latencies are the vendor DT values - measure before freezing. Tick
broadcast under local-timer-stop must be verified on hardware.

Validation: full RELEASE build; built DSDT decodes 8x _LPI with both
states and correct FFH addresses. Hardware verification pending (the
v13 boot: cpuidle states present, usage counts increasing, wake
sources intact).
